# TypeScript

- Strict compiler options; no ignored TS errors; no `any` without a short justified comment.
- Prefer explicit names, small functions, immutable data where practical.
- Share types via `packages/*` or `ipc-contracts` — do not duplicate DTOs.
- Do not add extra type/wrapper layers for a single call site.
- Exhaustive handling for status/error unions where feasible.
- Do not disable lint rules without documenting why adjacent to the disable comment.
